## Risks
- noinline changes the marked ELF layout; csr (opcode) + pc (symbol-name) triggers
  are layout-agnostic.
- icount-mode targets must fit in one program lifetime; the prefix + one
  kernel call (~35K insns) is the budget. Targets >35K will run past _exit
  and fail the kernel-range assertion.
- simpoint profile/slice cover the whole program including the startup
  prefix, which dominates the insn count when the kernel runs only once.

